# Citation File Format 1.2.0 — https://citation-file-format.github.io
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS (NMI-3). Nature Methods requires a citation file, a data-availability statement and
# a code/data DOI. The absence was conspicuous rather than neutral: this repository cites OTHER people's
# DOIs correctly throughout (10.5281/zenodo.7859480 for WholeCellEcoliRelease v3.0.1, 10.5281/zenodo.8284223
# for PRECISE-1K, 10.1093/nar/gkad435), so archiving everyone else's work and none of our own is a visible
# asymmetry.
#
# WHAT IS STILL MISSING, named here rather than guessed at:
#   * `doi:` — needs a Zenodo (or equivalent) deposit, which only the repository owner can make. It is left
#     OUT rather than filled with a plausible-looking identifier: a wrong DOI resolves to someone else's
#     work, which is worse than no DOI.
#   * co-authors — authorship is the owner's call and not a thing to infer from a commit log. The one author
#     below is the copyright holder named in LICENSE.
#   * ORCID — not recorded anywhere in this repository, so it is not asserted here.
#   * the DATA-AVAILABILITY statement is deliberately not written yet: its wording depends on the pending
#     upstream-licence question for the model-derived parquet in `data/manifest/` (see NMI-5), and a
#     statement that answers that question before the licensor does would be the wrong kind of commitment.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Cellarium, please cite it as below."
title: Cellarium
abstract: >-
  A glass box over whole-cell reasoning. A blind Socratic Council frames a question about Escherichia coli
  into a falsifiable hypothesis without seeing the data; a grounded agent then tests it against real
  whole-cell simulations and the published literature, and proposes experiments for human approval. Every
  number carries its provenance, and the agent never launches a simulation on its own.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Nikolados
    given-names: Evangelos-Marios
version: 0.1.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/evanniko1/cellarium"
keywords:
  - whole-cell model
  - Escherichia coli
  - agentic workbench
  - provenance
  - falsifiability
  - large language models
# The simulator Cellarium runs on is a separate work under its own terms, and the corpus is published
# separately from the code. Both are recorded as references so a citation of Cellarium does not read as a
# citation of them.
references:
  - type: software
    title: Whole-Cell Model of Escherichia coli (WholeCellEcoliRelease)
    authors:
      - name: Covert Lab, Stanford University
    doi: 10.5281/zenodo.7859480
    version: 3.0.1
    notes: >-
      Obtained separately under Stanford's academic licence; Cellarium's own MIT licence does not cover it.
  - type: data
    title: cellarium-corpus
    authors:
      - family-names: Nikolados
        given-names: Evangelos-Marios
    url: "https://huggingface.co/datasets/evanniko1/cellarium-corpus"
    notes: >-
      The simulation corpus Cellarium reads. Published under `license: other` because it is derived from a
      model under non-commercial academic terms; the in-tree manifest under `data/manifest/` is the same
      category of data and its licence wording is under review.
